The first question is "are you new", not "which provider"
=========================================================

The first-run screen opened with "Where should the models run?" — a question a person meeting the app
for the first time cannot answer, and one a person who already runs three of these should not have to.

So it asks the question that actually decides the experience:

  **Are you new to QuixiDesk?**
  - *Yes* — where the models run, then how they get there. Two questions, nothing assumed.
  - *No* — one table with the four things that matter: provider, key, model, browser. Anything left
    blank stays unset, and everything else lives in Settings.

Both paths end in the same working app; the difference is how much a person has to read to get there.
Neither is a commitment, and neither writes a provider the user did not choose.

Also in this patch, from the same session's screen-time:

  * the sidebar brand is one line with an ellipsis instead of a sentence, because "Published edition ·
    GITHUB · no personal data, no keys" inside a 228px column pushed the block down over the
    navigation and the New instance button
  * two narrow-window breakpoints tighten the top bar — smaller chips at 1200px, shorter labels and no
    caret at 1040px — so the two chips shrink before they collide with the buttons beside them

